      "claim": "Most of the Context section's line numbers are stale, by a consistent amount (roughly 21-23 lines), in files the spec already touches: `saffron/cell/session.py:1897-1898` (the `_drive_cell` network/critic_network binding) is actually at 1920-1921, `:1408-1410` (the gate-subnet sweep) is actually at 1431-1433, `:1328`/`:1364` (comments naming `saffron-cells`) are actually at 1351/1387, `proxy_address` is at `session.py:1015` not `992-996`, and `DESIGN.md:626-628` (the §5.1 one-time block) is actually at 647-650. This is pure drift from unrelated commits landing between `60f8b3f5` (where the spec says it read line numbers) and the base commit `cf3db797`, not a correctness problem: every passage is still textually accurate at its new location, and `saffron/cell/proxy.py` and `saffron/end_review.py` have zero drift (diff empty between the two commits) so their line citations are exact. Since the Problem/Notes sections that actually drive the build do not depend on these specific line numbers, this is not a blocker, but a literal check of \"is every sentence about the current code true at this snapshot\" does turn up several technically-false line citations, all in files the spec will edit anyway.",
