      "claim": "This is already SA-0269's second attempt, and that context is not visible from the spec file itself. `docs/backlog/b-ca3bc6-*.md` records that a prior revision of this same spec id ran in the spec loop on 2026-10-12 and ended `EXHAUSTED` at $41.03 against a $36 budget after three gate attempts, because its `touches` omitted `tests/test_sigterm.py` (commit `a7fea332`). The commit under review here is exactly the fix for that: `tests/test_sigterm.py` is now in `touches`, `budget_usd` rose from 36 to 52, and `max_turns` rose from 180 to 240, with a new \"Notes for the agent\" paragraph pointing at `tests/test_sigterm.py:20,42-43`, which I verified is accurate (the file does import `CRITIC_NETWORK` and does assert `removed:network:saffron-cells` in its teardown order at those exact lines, undrifted). This is not a defect in the spec text, but the operator should know, before paying for a second attempt, that the first one already spent roughly $41 and that this revision's only change versus the version that failed is the touches/budget/turns fix.",
