      "claim": "DESIGN.md's K=1 claim is correct but easy to misread. The spec says \"K stays 1 (DESIGN.md §4.2.1).\" Elsewhere in DESIGN.md, in an earlier paragraph adjacent to but not inside §4.2.1, there is old prose discussing \"Concurrency cap K = 3\" as a design target. §4.2.1 itself explicitly lists \"K > 1\" among what is \"still deferred,\" so the spec's claim is true, but a shallow grep against DESIGN.md for \"K\" would surface the K=3 passage first and could cause an unnecessary double-take. No action is needed; this is purely a note for whoever double-checks the citation.",
